# dist/ is generated — EXCEPT page.html, which is the deliverable: the whole
# recovery tool as one committed file a holder can open from a USB stick. An
# ignored artifact is a 404 for everyone but the machine that built it, which is
# the defect C7b exists to remove.
#
# THE FIRST LINE IS NOT DECORATION. packages/.gitignore (one level up) excludes
# `dist/` as a DIRECTORY, and git does not descend into an excluded directory —
# so a bare `!dist/page.html` here is inert and the artifact stays invisible.
# Re-including the directory, then ignoring its contents, then re-including the
# one file, is the only ordering that works. Check it the way that cannot be
# misread: `git ls-files dist/page.html` prints the path once it is committed.
# test/page-bundle.test.ts asserts exactly that, because a negated
# `git check-ignore -v` still exits 0 and reads like an ignore.
!dist/
dist/*
!dist/page.html
